# Personal Clinical Record – project rules

## Product
- Personal clinical record inspired by hospital NIS/EHR — **not** a medical device, clinical decision-support, or legally maintained provider documentation.
- Do **not** diagnose, recommend treatment changes, or invent clinical guidance.
- MVP: one admin account + one active patient; data model always includes `patientId` for multi-patient later.
- Equal targets: desktop and iPhone (PWA). UI language: Czech. Default TZ: `Europe/Prague`.
- No mandatory cloud analytics/telemetry; no sending health data to third parties.

## Source of truth
- Read `README.md`, `docs/PRD.md`, `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`, `docs/DATA_MODEL.md`, `docs/UX_UI_SPEC.md`, `docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md`, `docs/app-plan.md`, `DEPLOY.md` before coding.
- Follow phases in `docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` as adjusted by Gate decisions in `docs/app-plan.md`.
- Do **not** invent requirements. Escalate unknowns upward; record open questions instead of guessing.
- Do **not** implement the whole product in one pass.

## Gate decisions (authoritative, 2026-11-14)
1. `health.combatostrich.dev` = **full app + DB** on combat-server.
2. Use **existing Postgres** on the server; Matěj creates DB user + database; **public HTTPS** yes (he owns certs).
3. Repo nginx template = **reverse proxy to Next** immediately; Matěj deploys conf himself.
4. MVP includes **full symptom diary with scales**.
5. Lab / fluids in quick-add: **do not hide** — show as available/roadmap (no fake full modules).
6. Documents: **backup/export only** for now — **no Documents nav agenda** in MVP.
7. **Dark mode from Phase 1**.
8. Patient: add **contact / preferred address form / default weight**; define **User/Account** in DATA_MODEL (follow-up docs task).
9. Corrections: **update in place** + `AuditEvent` with before/after (same DB transaction).
10. Plan lives in GitHub `docs/app-plan.md`.
11. This file (`.cursor/rules/project.mdc`) is required.
12. Commits go **straight to `main`** (no PR required unless explicitly asked).
13. Agents **never** touch live nginx/SSL — **templates only** under `nginx/`.

## Git / deploy
- One user prompt change set = **one commit** on `main`.
- Public repo: never commit real personal/health data, secrets, backups, or production dumps.
- Deploy path: `/var/webserver/health.combatostrich.dev` — sync via `scripts/pull-main.sh` / cron (see `DEPLOY.md`).
- Agents do not configure live reverse proxy or certificates.

## Implementation habits
- Stack: Next.js App Router, React, TypeScript, Tailwind, shadcn/ui, Lucide, Recharts, PostgreSQL, Prisma, Zod, React Hook Form, pnpm, PWA (shell-only SW cache).
- Use current stable library versions; lock in lockfile; no unverified beta/canary.
- After each phase: `pnpm lint`, `pnpm typecheck`, relevant tests — fix before continuing.
- Seed/fixtures: obviously fictional data only.
- Server-authoritative writes; forms show saving / saved / failed; never claim “saved” without server confirmation.
- No private clinical data in logs, `localStorage`, or service-worker Cache Storage.
- Clinical mutations create `AuditEvent` in the same transaction; corrections = in-place update + before/after audit.
- Soft-delete only for config/drafts; do not silently rewrite clinical history without audit.

## Out of scope until later phases
- Full lab / fluid-balance / procedures / multi-patient / caregiver roles modules (Phase 9), except roadmap affordances explicitly allowed (e.g. visible quick-add items).
- Live server nginx/SSL changes.
- Rewriting product docs wholesale without an assigned docs task.
